Under linear feedback $\mathbf{u} = \mathbf{K}\boldsymbol{\epsilon}$, the instantaneous control power is $P_{\mathrm{ctrl}} = \mathbf{u}^T \mathbf{R} \mathbf{u} = \boldsymbol{\epsilon}^T \mathbf{K}^T \mathbf{R} \mathbf{K} \boldsymbol{\epsilon}$. Taking the expectation over the steady-state distribution of $\boldsymbol{\epsilon}$ yields

