Proof. The drift floor corresponds to the steady-state variance when $c$ is maximized by optimal control. The Lyapunov inequality must hold at the optimum, so $\operatorname{tr}(\mathbf{\Sigma}^T \mathbf{P} \mathbf{\Sigma})$ is the unavoidable noise contribution. Setting $c$ to its maximum achievable value under actuator constraints yields $\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}^2 = \operatorname{tr}(\mathbf{\Sigma}^T \mathbf{P} \mathbf{\Sigma})/c$. $\square$

