For a block of $R$ bits protected by an $[n,k,d]$-code (simplified to a binary symmetric channel with flip probability $p_{\mathrm{flip}}$ per bit per interval $\Delta t$), the probability of uncorrectable error is bounded by the probability that more than $t_{\mathrm{corr}} = \lfloor (d-1)/2 \rfloor$ bits are corrupted. Using the union bound,

